A||||10||kitcar||GTP 3.8 supercharge help||||1||
Z||000000||kitcar||04-23-2001||06:20 PM||||I heard the 98 and up GTP engine will bolt into the fiero.  Is this true?  The GTP engine is a L67 with a 3.8 supercharger.<P>Has anyone done this?  How much would it cost of installing a new engine?<BR>Sorry with the questions, im making a kit right now and adding a new engine, and was wondering the price.<P>Also if my car weighs 2,300lbs and i have a 3.8 superchargerd engine in it, what would i run in the 1/4 and 0-60 time??? anyone<BR>thanks<BR>jake||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||04-23-2001||06:48 PM||||Pick up the latest issue of Hot Rod Magazine and you will see Phil's Supercharged 3800 fiero. This is a very common engine swap and there are a few vendors here that sell kits or install the engines for you. <P>I know Design One systems sells a kit and I think Chris West sells some motor mounts and headers too.<P> <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.designonesystems.com/</A> <P>Look here too. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||04-23-2001||06:55 PM||||Design One sells Turbocharger kits for the fiero. ACE sells the 3800 kit I talked about. <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||kitcar||04-23-2001||07:00 PM||||88formula, thanks for the reply...i jsut got off the phone with <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.designonesystems.com/</A>  and they said they do not sell the 3.8 conversion kit.  The mainly deal with the northstar.  I am going to pick up the new hot rod mag to see who does sell this setup.  After i buy the converstion kit, how much would it cost to be installed and the new engine be put in?  <P>If anyone could, what would be my 1/4 time and 0-60 time if my car weighs 2,300lbs with a 3.8 supercharged engine in it.<BR>thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||04-23-2001||07:25 PM||||Sorry it is ACE that sells the kit. I think Phil's car weights around 2800 lbs. He will probably read this post and correct me but that is what my formula weighs. How did you get your car down to 2300 lbs.?<P>The supercharged 3800 engine in a 2800 lb. fiero will do mid thirteen second quarter mile times or better depending on how much traction you can get.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||kitcar||04-23-2001||07:28 PM||||88formula, the reason i have no weight is because i have a whole new body kit on the car.  LOT lighter!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||04-23-2001||07:42 PM||||How much does the fiero body weigh? <P>I ran a simulation for you and with a 2800 lb. car and the supercharged 3800 engine with the smaller pulley (280 horsepower) you would go 0-60 mph in a traction limited 5 seconds and run the quarter mile in 13.1 seconds @ 107.7 mph. This is if you have the five speed getrag transmission and stock size tires.<P>If your car really weighs only 2300 lbs. than your car would go 0-60 mph in 4.4 seconds and run the quarter mile in 12.34 @ 114.7 mph. You would have to launch at a very low 1000 rpm and you would still have tones of tire spin off the line.<P>I don't have the exact camshaft specifications on this engine so I used something that I think will be close. I usually do simulations for the 3.4, 3.1, and 2.8 guys because I have so much information on those engines.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||04-23-2001||09:52 PM||||My car weighs( inc. my 200 lb lard butt) 3068 lbs. My conversion was done by ACE and so far 42000 trouble free miles- well not entirely true - having trouble finding a clutch to hold back the mighty sc3800 (small pulley)||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||04-23-2001||11:25 PM||||I'm sure Phil is expecting this, and no disrespet to his awesome ride, but shop around before you give ACE your money. My dad had his conversion done by ACE. Not to get into too many gory details, their engineering and business ethic left me unimpressed. Call West Coast Fieros.<BR>These guys are hard core! <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||RobertVol||04-24-2001||04:26 PM||||And this is no disrespect to Stimp at all either...(By the way Stimp I am getting with you on that Sub in the footwell soon <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>But mine ws done by ACE. I had no problems what so ever. There was few things that had to be worked out but they helped me out all the way. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||04-24-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>My car weighs( inc. my 200 lb lard butt) 3068 lbs. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Phil! What does that make me? I weigh 210!! hehe<P>Guess you are not coming to Alabama this weekend? I would love to see that car for real. Finally got my T-top and I'm hoping to do that conversion as well!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
